  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWhile implementing servo/servo#50044, I noticed that [nearest inclusive target popover](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#nearest-inclusive-target-popover) has no return value for the case where no node has a matching target popover.\n\nThe algorithm walks up the flat tree and only return early when it finds a node with an open target popover in the Auto state or the Hint state. If the loop finishes without finding such a node, nothing says what to return.\n\nI would suggest adding a final return step after the loop. Something like:\n\n> 3. Return null.",
